# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in the values. `.env` is gitignored.
#
#   cp .env.example .env

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Contact form — EmailJS
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Three identifiers, from https://dashboard.emailjs.com
#
#   Service ID   → Email Services  (the Gmail/Workspace connection)
#   Template ID  → Email Templates
#   Public Key   → Account → General → API Keys
#
# All three are public by design: EmailJS runs in the browser, so every site
# using it ships these in its page source, exactly like a reCAPTCHA site key.
# None of them can read past submissions.
#
# ⚠️  BECAUSE THEY ARE PUBLIC, DO THIS OR THE QUOTA IS OPEN TO ANYONE:
#     EmailJS dashboard → Account → Security → turn on "Use Allowed List" and
#     add jpmediagroups.com. Without it, somebody can paste these keys into
#     their own page and send mail through this account until the quota is gone.
#
# Also set all three in Vercel → Settings → Environment Variables, for
# Production, Preview and Development. Variables that only exist locally mean
# the live form reports "not configured yet" while it works on your machine.
#
# Any one of them missing and the form refuses to send rather than pretending.
PUBLIC_EMAILJS_SERVICE_ID=
PUBLIC_EMAILJS_TEMPLATE_ID=
PUBLIC_EMAILJS_PUBLIC_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The EmailJS template must match the form's field names
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# `sendForm` turns every field's `name` attribute into a template variable.
# Rename a field in src/pages/contact.astro without renaming it in the
# dashboard and the send still succeeds — the email just arrives blank.
#
# The template needs these variables:
#
#   {{name}}        the sender's name
#   {{email}}       the sender's email
#   {{discipline}}  what they picked from the dropdown
#   {{message}}     the brief itself
#   {{subject}}     written by the script as "New project brief — <name>"
#
# In the template settings:
#
#   Subject   → {{subject}}
#   To Email  → contact@jpmediagroups.com
#   Reply To  → {{email}}       ← without this, replying in Gmail answers
#                                 EmailJS instead of the client
#
# A content body that works:
#
#   From: {{name}} <{{email}}>
#   Interested in: {{discipline}}
#
#   {{message}}
